"""Unselected native storm/control questions, not adopted procedures."""
IDS = ['cosmic-implosion', 'frozen-eternity', 'hellstorm',
       'storm-of-vengeance', 'thunder-wrath', 'storm-cage']
TIERS = {
 'cosmic-implosion': ('B', 'Existing persistent-field and inward-pull contracts provide a bounded comparison; exact geometry, continued concentration and repeated magnitude still require an explicit local choice.'),
 'frozen-eternity': ('C', 'Time stop and no action leave materially different action, movement, incoming-effect and personal-clock interpretations; these cannot be silently replaced by Paralyzed.'),
 'hellstorm': ('B', 'Printed three-round fire pulses can use expressly extended existing damage/clock interfaces once the 100-foot geometry and exactly three events are selected.'),
 'storm-of-vengeance': ('C', 'The native varied multiround storm has no exact damage table or geometry and contradicts Instantaneous metadata; a complete substantive schedule is required.'),
 'thunder-wrath': ('C', 'Five strikes per round requires explicit event ownership, control expenditure, targeting and clocks without inheriting Storm Sphere’s one-bolt ceiling.'),
 'storm-cage': ('C', 'Cannot escape is a substantive containment promise; admission, teleport/forced movement, suppression and recurring damage require a distinct boundary/lifecycle contract.')}

Q = [
 ('RS9-Q01', IDS,
  'All six have actual rank9/minimum class level17/base26RP access. Five are Mage/Wizard Evocation; Storm Cage separately includes Druid Conjuration. Core supplies Action and components but not complete recipient procedures.',
  'A: retain every actual route and use ordinary paid class-qualified commitment/Ready interfaces. B: propose a specific source-supported route correction with complete before/after evidence.',
  'Recommend A. Preserve native placements, acquired repertoire, actual class focus/components, price/cadence, concentration replacement and counters. Cosmic Implosion alone prints V/S/M/F; the others V/S/F. Same rank or name does not grant access, a generic upcast, a second payment at Ready release or an autonomous summoned-creature turn. All options remain unselected.'),
 ('RS9-Q02', IDS,
  'The applied P20/DC25 contracts have expressly limited scopes. Their pulse clocks, family exposure, origin attacks and root snapshots are not automatic global rules.',
  'A: expressly select the relevant named clauses for each new spell, adding only its necessary local deltas. B: author a fully specified alternative and identify the concrete source conflict.',
  'Recommend A where compatible. List exactly which damage events and continuing riders share a root, when original-owner Null is sampled, and which budgets survive suppression/recast/extra turns. Actual damage mitigation, temporary HP, Wounds, death and concentration use accepted stages. Null does not itself cancel movement, containment or temporal riders. Do not multiply roots to escape a source rule or merge separate strikes into one Wound event without selection.'),
 ('RS9-Q03', ['cosmic-implosion'],
  'Pull ALL creatures within100feet toward center; Core casting range100feet. Radius, center and 3D pull geometry are not equivalent to Flame Typhoon’s enemy-only horizontal cylinder.',
  'A: a fixed100-foot-radius sphere centered at a perceived point within100feet. B: a self-centered sphere. C: another full100-foot geometry with explicit rationale.',
  'Recommend A as NEW local geometry, with actual occupied-body intersection and center line of effect. Preserve all creatures, including allies/caster when genuinely inside; do not apply a perceived-hostile filter. Choose whether pull is 3D toward the center or horizontal toward an axis. Spell center visibility does not grant visibility of every area occupant. Resolve ceilings, underwater/unsupported centers and world clipping without reducing the radius.'),
 ('RS9-Q04', ['cosmic-implosion'],
  '15d10force accompanies inward pull, while Core concentration lasts up to one minute. Concentration alone does not establish repeated15d10 or the continuing benefit.',
  'A: an initial and scheduled recurring15d10/pull field under an expressly extended P20 pulse contract. B: one15d10 admission event followed by a specified continuing pull/control field. C: a precisely armed one-shot discharge sustained by concentration.',
  'Choose one complete positive lifecycle. A closely reuses Flame Typhoon but repeated15d10 is explicitly NEW and needs named selection, not inference. B must specify the useful continuing field and every later movement event. Preserve one-minute maximum if retaining Core concentration; any alternative duration is an explicit source reconciliation. Set creation, six-second or regular-marker cadence, final-exclusive expiry, source interruption, suppressed lost events and no catch-up. Never leave concentration with no authored effect.'),
 ('RS9-Q05', ['cosmic-implosion'],
  'No save, pull distance, damage-versus-motion order or collision treatment is printed.',
  'A: NEW STR save, full15d10 plus10-foot inward pull on failure, half and no pull on success, with damage then movement. B: another exact save/automatic resolution and finite pull amount.',
  'A is a reviewable comparison to Flame Typhoon, not an adopted rule. Preserve independent damage and movement defenses: force immunity does not automatically grant anchoring, and actual anchoring does not erase damage. State precise legal stopping, occupied-center arbitration and simultaneous recipients using real bodies; no arbitrary size immunity, crushing, body overlap or teleport. Retain actual support loss/Falling and movement already spent. Define eligibility after lethal damage or actual survival replacements.'),
 ('RS9-Q06', ['frozen-eternity'],
  'Native TIME STOP FOR ONE TARGET; NO ACTION FOR3ROUNDS. Neither text nor Core defines a complete temporal state.',
  'A: source-local temporal suspension of self-directed Action/Bonus Action/Reaction/movement with an explicitly defined incoming-effect policy. B: literal personal stasis with selected personal processes paused. C: narrow full-Action denial with other faculties retained, explicitly reconciling the time-stop phrase.',
  'Confer on the actual intended benefit before choosing. List senses, communication, consciousness, voluntary/forced movement, existing concentration, active defenses and item use separately. Do not silently substitute Frozen Tomb’s Paralyzed, add its attack-critical vulnerability/cold damage, or choose C merely because it is easier to implement. A/B must explain how escape saves and external world events remain possible; C must affirmatively resolve the source meaning rather than omit it.'),
 ('RS9-Q07', ['frozen-eternity'],
  'WIS SAVE ENDS and three rounds are explicit; initial admission, repeat-save markers and treatment of an underway turn are absent.',
  'A: NEW initial WIS, then actual future regular END saves, with a third-future-END maximum excluding an underway turn. B: initial WIS plus fixed six-second ending opportunities over18elapsed seconds. C: another exact original-marker contract preserving the printed upper bound.',
  'Select initial success/failure and repeat cadence, plus whether final expiry precedes a coincident save. Apply existing source-character/target/encounter whole-Action denial admission to actual hard control, spending once on establishment, not once per missed turn. The allowance does not silently shorten an admitted three-round application. Define attached/absent phases expressly using Control15 only as its accepted-but-unapplied comparison; do not inherit Dominate’s bridge or Dance’s different bridge by name.'),
 ('RS9-Q08', ['frozen-eternity'],
  'Literal personal time suspension could affect incoming damage, healing, poison, death/recovery, recharge and preexisting spell deadlines. Ordinary world/planar clocks otherwise continue.',
  'A: personal decisions stop but every existing external clock and event remains live. B: enumerate a bounded set of genuinely paused personal processes with exact suspension/resumption and incoming-event handling.',
  'For each category choose resolve-now, defer-exactly-once or ineligible; never delete unspecified events. If deferring, bind queue ownership, original source/Null snapshot, stale recipient identity, lethal ordering, concentration and overlapping freezes. Existing resource use and damage never rewind; time stop cannot create recharge/rest, extend another caster’s spell for free or fabricate caster turns. Pending ordinary Time Stop and Time Echo remain comparisons only. No named-plane clock exception follows.'),
 ('RS9-Q09', ['frozen-eternity'],
  'Suppression, ending saves, overlapping temporal sources and interrupted target phases can change availability without changing elapsed history.',
  'A: original deadline and ending saves continue through suppression, with only covered state expression suspended. B: a specifically authored stasis exception with full opposing-source and budget consequences.',
  'Recommend A unless selected literal stasis needs a concrete scoped exception. Preserve any actual paid commitments, spent Actions and control allowance. On resume do not supply missed turns, regenerate Reactions, reroll past saves or restore concentration already lost. Specify whether an already-committed attack/Ready release finishes and how newly legal target actions are scheduled. Require a useful positive time-stop case plus initial immunity/used-allowance and suppressed-save cases.'),
 ('RS9-Q10', ['hellstorm'],
  'Rain of fire OVER100FT and Core range100feet leave area shape, radius/diameter and overhead exposure undefined.',
  'A: NEW100-foot-radius vertical rain cylinder with a specified height. B:100-foot-diameter cylinder. C: a100-foot-radius sphere with exact manifestation and obstruction rules.',
  'Confer on the ambiguity; do not quietly halve the area. Fix a perceived center within range and real origin-to-body/roof line of effect. Define indoor/underground/underwater use and whether an actual sky opening is required. Preserve the full selected volume even beyond placement range, with all qualifying creatures rather than a hidden enemy filter. No infernal-plane identity follows from the name.'),
 ('RS9-Q11', ['hellstorm'],
  '8d10 PER ROUND FOR3ROUNDS supplies three damaging opportunities, not four; concentration is not printed.',
  'A: NEW three source pulses at establishment, +6s and +12s, expiry at+18s, no concentration. B: three actual regular-marker pulses with a preserved out-of-initiative equivalent. C: expressly add concentration with the same complete pulse count.',
  'Recommend A as a narrow elapsed-clock completion. Explicitly choose same-family recipient limits across overlapping owners/casts and coordinate source pulse epochs with numbered rounds. Entry, reentry, forced movement, extra turns or field resumption do not independently create a fourth event. Suppressed/unavailable pulses are lost under the selected contract and cannot bank. Countering before establishment produces no pulse; a committed pulse snapshot finishes under its selected source-ending ordering.'),
 ('RS9-Q12', ['hellstorm'],
  'The printed8d10fire has no save, immunity riders, ground ignition or independent terrain hazard.',
  'A: NEW DEX for full/half with one shared8d10 raw roll per pulse and ordinary real defenses. B: automatic damage or another fully specified resolution.',
  'A is proposed, not recovered source. Keep each qualifying pulse distinct for damage/temporaryHP/Wounds and concentration. Decide creature/object eligibility and obstruction at each pulse. Inferno Wave’s separately printed ground ignition is not automatically inherited. If environmental burning is chosen as NEW, include finite actual substrate, ignition, fuel and later independent physical-fire provenance; no free material, unnamed suffocation or magic dispel reversing existing physical damage.'),
 ('RS9-Q13', ['storm-of-vengeance'],
  'A MASSIVE STORM deals VARIOUS DAMAGE TYPES over MULTIPLE ROUNDS; Core Instantaneous conflicts and no exact amounts/types/schedule exist.',
  'A: author one finite native multistage table with a different selected typed event at each stage. B: author a complete multitype pulse repeated over a finite duration, with exact component allocation.',
  'Recommend A, requiring the full table before any operational acceptance: every stage’s offset, type, dice, save/success, recipients and optional rider. A concrete discussion candidate is three stages at0/6/12s using8d10lightning/8d10cold/8d10thunder respectively, expiry18s; all those numbers/types are NEW and not balance-approved. Do not import a foreign ten-round storm table, quietly make one blast, or omit the native variety. GPT must select or replace the proposal with equally complete positive behavior.'),
 ('RS9-Q14', ['storm-of-vengeance'],
  'Massive has no defined dimensions; Core supplies120-foot casting range, not an area size. A storm may have distinct visible volume and damage origins.',
  'A: NEW fixed100-foot-radius,60-foot-high cylinder at a supported point within120feet. B: another explicit large3D geometry retaining the massive-storm benefit.',
  'A is a concrete proposal, not authority. Set vertical origin, full body intersections, roof/cover/sky and indoor behavior. Specify each stage’s ray or volume origins without revealing hidden occupants. Allcreatures versus perceived selected recipients must be explicit. No camera clipping, target-count convenience cap or silent area reduction. A fixed storm need not follow a caster; any movement must have its own exact route/speed/cost/occupied-volume rules.'),
 ('RS9-Q15', ['storm-of-vengeance'],
  'No concentration/control, repeated-cast conflict or event budget is given for the multiround storm.',
  'A: NEW concentration for the entire finite staged lifetime; source-relative elapsed stages with per-stage recipient history. B: finite nonconcentration stages with explicit overlapping-source arbitration.',
  'Recommend A for discussion, clearly adding concentration rather than falsely reading it from Core. Bind stages to real world time and source ID, no new caster turn, no repeated RP/cadence payments. Decide same-family overlap without erasing genuinely different scheduled types. State a stage committed before source ending versus later stages, suppression skips, source/recipient immunity, death/form changes and exact original expiry. No indefinitely autonomous weather engine.'),
 ('RS9-Q16', ['storm-of-vengeance'],
  'Storm language does not specify wind, obscurement, difficult terrain, rain volume, lightning conduction, structural damage or lasting weather.',
  'A: a visible/audible bounded storm whose selected damage table is its mechanical effect. B: add separately enumerated finite environment components with actual geometry and material consequences.',
  'Choose the intended useful manifestation explicitly. A must retain varied multiround storm damage; B must supply real wind force/movement, visibility, liquid/material quantities or destruction only where chosen. Pending Control Weather, Earthquake and Absolute Silence do not supply permissions. Lightning is not thunder: a silence source may affect a genuinely thunder component only under its own selected scope, not every storm attack. No inferred faction deity or cosmological vengeance authority.'),
 ('RS9-Q17', ['thunder-wrath'],
  'Storm CLOUD strikes5TIMES PER ROUND for6d6LIGHTNING; Core120feet/Instantaneous conflicts with a continuing cloud.',
  'A: NEW fixed cloud with a finite three-round/18second lifetime and concentration. B: another exact finite duration/geometry and concentration choice retaining five strikes each eligible round.',
  'Specify cloud dimensions, origin, placement range and strike range separately; a comparison is a20-foot-radius cloud at a legal point within120feet, striking within60feet of its center. All these dimensions/lifetime are NEW. Do not inherit Storm Sphere’s one-bolt ceiling or turn five strikes into five dice. Preserve lightning type despite the title. Do not fabricate a summoned creature, independent resources or weather-plane source.'),
 ('RS9-Q18', ['thunder-wrath'],
  'No target-allocation rule, attack/save procedure or repeat-target limit exists for the five strikes.',
  'A: NEW five distinct ranged spell attacks, each6d6lightning, targets declared before the group resolves; repeated targets permitted. B: five source pulses with independent chosen saves and exact allocation. C: another complete five-strike procedure.',
  'Recommend A for review, extending Storm Sphere’s actual center-origin attack contract expressly. Keep five separate events with actual cover, owner restrictions, critical rules, defense consumption and source-specific hit hooks. State what happens if an earlier strike kills/changes a later declared target; no post-roll retargeting or free information. If distinct-target-only is selected, disclose the lost single-target capability as a NEW restriction, not native text. Shared versus per-strike RNG must be fixed.'),
 ('RS9-Q19', ['thunder-wrath'],
  'Five strikes per round leaves control expenditure, creation-round eligibility, numbering and banked opportunities unresolved.',
  'A: one real Bonus Action on an eligible regular turn commands a group of five. B: each source-relative six-second pulse automatically issues a predeclared complete five-strike group. C: another explicitly budgeted control contract.',
  'Select the substantive control model before case authorship. A needs an actually available Bonus Action, genuine hostile initiative and an expressly chosen maximum across recasts/extra turns; it cannot charge five Bonus Actions or silently allow only one strike. B needs exact targeting and no autonomous hidden-foe knowledge. Define original pulse epochs versus numbered-round boundaries to prevent duplicate groups or a fourth group in a three-round source. Unused opportunities expire without banking or extra owner Actions.'),
 ('RS9-Q20', ['thunder-wrath'],
  'A committed five-strike group can encounter target death, newly lost concentration, suppression, owner incapacity or movement between strikes.',
  'A: finish the entire already-committed snapshot group, then end future groups. B: preserve five ordered separately interruptible strike commitments with explicit legality rechecks and spent opportunities.',
  'Confer on this real ordering choice rather than copying a one-bolt example. Preserve all committed costs, original damage-root provenance and exact sequential recipient state. Damage absorption, Wounds and concentration remain per actual event. Say precisely which later strikes fail after owner/source ending and whether missed/invalid strikes still occupy slots. Suppression/expiry cannot refill spent group history, relocate cloud or restart the duration.'),
 ('RS9-Q21', ['storm-cage'],
  'Trap ONE CREATURE in an electrical field. No target size, initial save, field shape or body-following rule is printed.',
  'A: NEW one perceived creature within120feet, initial DEX or STR admission save, fixed whole-body containment region. B: an attached source-owned confinement state with exact world boundary semantics.',
  'Choose the save and success behavior explicitly; do not add arbitrary Huge immunity. Define the whole actual occupied body at establishment, field clearance, passengers/carried objects, form/size changes and legal growth. An electrical field is not automatically a solid cage object with HP or a creature. Existing Wall of Force occupancy rules are comparison only; no bisection, crushing, free displacement or implicit prison-plane admission.'),
 ('RS9-Q22', ['storm-cage'],
  '8d6PERROUND/CANNOTESCAPE conflicts with Core Instantaneous and has no finite endpoint.',
  'A: NEW concentration up to18seconds with creation/+6/+12s damage. B: NEW concentration up to60seconds with a full finite pulse schedule. C: another expressly chosen duration and clock contract.',
  'Choose duration substantively; neither three rounds nor one minute is native. Preserve repeated8d6 and meaningful confinement for the selected whole lifetime. Set original deadline, pulse count, source-ending ordering and family conflict. Decide whether hard-control admission applies to any authored full-Action denial; confinement alone must not be mislabeled full Action denial if meaningful attacks/actions remain available. Never suppress all positive confinement as an unspecified-adapter rejection.'),
 ('RS9-Q23', ['storm-cage'],
  'CANNOT ESCAPE is stronger than ordinary movement restraint, but does not enumerate teleport, forced movement, attacks or outside intervention.',
  'A: a source-local boundary blocks voluntary movement, outside forced movement and teleport endpoints that would remove the prisoner while active, retaining lawful actions inside. B: a precisely enumerated different containment rule that expressly reconciles any allowed escape with the native promise.',
  'Recommend A for discussion, with a dedicated endpoint constraint rather than an invented teleport path. Specify whether the whole enclosure may move and whether outside allies can attack, heal, pull or carry the target; define targeting/line-of-effect crossing separately from body crossing. No routine repeat-save escape or generic helper-cutting fallback is printed. Actual dispel, source ending and suppression may remove containment, but their precise partial-boundary/resumption consequences require selection. Do not quietly substitute Restrained.'),
 ('RS9-Q24', ['storm-cage'],
  'Electrical8d6perround does not state whether damage saves, immunity, Null or suppression also release the trapped creature.',
  'A: explicitly select lightning damage with independently admitted containment; damage defenses do not by themselves release the prisoner. B: select an expressly coupled field rule with complete outcomes.',
  'Recommend A. Select initial versus later damage saves, full/half/none results and exactly one actual event per eligible pulse. Actual lightning immunity/temporaryHP/Null may change damage without ending an independent boundary. Distinguish source-wide and recipient-local suppression; preserve clocks and spent histories. If a real suppressed opening allows exit, determine whether this source ends permanently or can resume only around a still-contained clear body; no retroactive recapture, cutting or teleport back. Require useful positive containment and damage cases, not only rejections.'),
 ('RS9-Q25', IDS,
  'The full sources have no earlier complete operational cases for these identities; hash checks cannot prove newly chosen outcomes.',
  'A: after explicit decisions, author at least two complete source-qualified cases per spell plus every materially different timing/defense branch. B: retain an individually named content-dependent branch as conditional with its missing actual prerequisite.',
  'Use A with B only for genuine unavailable content. Each case needs actual access/repertoire/owner body, components/RP/cadence, clocks, occupied geometry, source IDs, full RNG inputs, intermediate damage/movement/control transitions and final state. Include five real Thunder Wrath strikes; all three Hellstorm pulses; a complete varied Vengeance schedule; full three-round Frozen Eternity maximum and its escape; actual Cage trapping/escape-prevention; and useful Cosmic pull/continuation. Preserve originals and indicate authored arithmetic separately from runtime, human play, balance, cosmology and release gates.')
